    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0408" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.74/165: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-31T20:00:00-03:00">January 31, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. As reported in Embassy’s telegram 267 of January 29, 12 a.m.,<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d350-f1"/> Transradio has informed the Mission that upon the
                    Argentine Government’s instructions its direct radio circuits with Axis
                    territory were severed at approximately 12 noon January 29. Radiar<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d350-f2"/> which had no direct circuits but which was able to
                    transmit messages through Spain to Axis territory reports that in accordance
                    with instructions its services were discontinued at about 4 p.m., January 29.
                    This is in connection with telegram 369, January 31, 12 a.m. from Rio.<anchor
                        n="64" xml:id="d350-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Rio.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="62" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f2" n="63" xml:id="d350-f2-content">
                <p>Sociedad Anónima Radio Argentina, which appears to have been owned by All America
                    Cables.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f3" n="64" xml:id="d350-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that radio communication between Argentina and the Axis
                    was still in effect (862.20210/2722).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
